---
// About copy from the master copy doc (hero thesis + about-page copy).
// Headline uses the hero thesis line; body uses the about-page intro and the
// two subsections (Our Connection to the Block / Designed for Venice).
// NOTE: rough first pass on presentation — copy is linked up, layout to be
// refined.
---

<section id="about" class="relative px-5 md:px-10 py-24 md:py-36">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="font-[var(--font-display)] uppercase font-black leading-[0.88] text-[clamp(2.25rem,6vw,4.75rem)] ink-stamp mb-10">
      Born from the neighborhood,<br />not dropped into it.
    </h2>

    <p class="text-lg md:text-2xl leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch] mb-14">
      Blockprint is a block party on Abbot Kinney, built from the block up. On
      August 22 the block transforms into a shared stage for electronic music,
      local art, food, and Venice culture.
    </p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-14">
      <div>
        <p class="section-marker section-marker--head mb-3">Our Connection to the Block</p>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch]">
          Blockprint grew out of The Cook's Garden, an urban farm owned by the
          co-founder's family that has been part of the boulevard's fabric for
          over a decade. When COVID threatened its survival, small,
          community-first music gatherings became the foundation for Blockprint.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="section-marker section-marker--head mb-3">Designed for Venice</p>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch]">
          The experience is woven into the fabric of Abbot Kinney. Businesses
          stay open. The street stays alive. Blockprint is built to feel like an
          elevated day on the boulevard.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-bp-pink-deep font-semibold text-lg md:text-xl mt-14">
      August 22, 2026 · 3–9 PM · Abbot Kinney Blvd · 21 and over.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
